{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Siren Lead",
 "category": "Leads and stabs",
 "text": "Sound: the wailing siren of big beat and rave tracks: a bright tone sweeping up and down by itself, echoing off into the distance.\n\nHow it's built: a triangle LFO into the oscillator's FM swings the pitch up and down (FM sets how far: half an octave either way here); the saw goes through a fairly open Ladder filter; the Delay's echoes bounce left and right.\n\nPlay: hold one high note.\n\nTweak: the LFO's RATE (slow wail to fast warble), the oscillator's FM (the size of the swing), the LFO's WAVE (Saw up for a repeating rise), the delay's FEEDBACK.",
